ormed.  Another rightward-pointing arrow then connects 'reverse' to the out=
put string 'racecar', also enclosed in double quotes, positioned on the rig=
ht.  The arrangement visually depicts the transformation of the input strin=
g 'racecar' into its reversed form, 'racecar,' through the application of t=
he 'reverse' function.  The entire diagram is linear, showing a clear, unid=
irectional flow of data from input to output via a clearly labeled process.=
" loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"263" height=3D"25" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=
=3D"1" style=3D"color:transparent" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/images/cou=
